kando (3.0.1-1nano) unstable; urgency=low

  * New upstream bugfix release
    - Fixed an issue where a single invalid theme.json5 file prevented the menu
      and settings from loading. Thanks to @hippi345 for the fix!
    - Fixed an issue on macOS where the app picker showed duplicate entries
      (e.g. "Siri") which multiplied with each search. Thanks to @skanpaul
      for the fix!
    - Fixed an issue on macOS where it was possible to resize the menu window
      with the mouse. Thanks to @rome-xi for the fix!
    - Fixed a regression on KDE Wayland 6.3 which would cause the shortcut
      settings of System Settings to open every time Kando was started. Thanks
      to @Tailszefox for the fix!
    - CMD+A can now be used to select text in input fields on macOS.
    - Fixed an issue on KDE where the Flatpak version of Kando would not connect
      to the KWin integration plugin.
    - Fixed several issues related the "Pointer fallback position" on
      wlroots-based compositors like Niri. Thanks to @presianbg for the fix!
    - Fixed a crash on wlroots-based Wayland compositors which send the
      foreign-toplevel parent event for every window. Thanks to @wl-chuang
      for the fix!

 -- Christopher Roy Bratusek <nano@jpberlin.de>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:20:09 +0100

